  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Mount Ulawun Volcano Eruption-Affected Communities in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 20 November 2023, Mount Ulawun volcano on the border of the West New Britain (WNB) and East New Britain (ENB) provinces in Papua New Guinea erupted, spewing ash plumes. The volcano eruption caused mass displacement across the affected areas. To address identified immediate needs, a multisectoral humanitarian response is required. IOM&apos;s operational objective is to scale up and expand a holistic emergency response to the immediate and emerging needs of volcano affected populations. Building directly on its existing field presence and portfolio, IOM is responding to the immediate humanitarian needs by providing emergency assistance using a multisectoral and people-centred approach focusing on Shelter/Non-Food Items (NFIs), Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), with protection mainstreamed. Also, IOM seeks to provide logistics support to the government in deploying field assessment teams as well as improve the living conditions in the internally displaced persons&#x2019; villages of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
